WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.602
The module starts with the shape itself.

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:07.077
Then we will pivot long data to wide form.

00:00:07.077 --> 00:00:10.437
After that, we will unpivot wide data back to long form.

00:00:10.437 --> 00:00:14.452
Next comes the most important safeguard: grain.

00:00:14.452 --> 00:00:21.352
Finally, we validate totals and choose the output shape that best serves the downstream use.

00:00:21.352 --> 00:00:26.397
Keep a real project in mind as we work through this section—for example,

00:00:26.397 --> 00:00:31.762
a BI dashboard turning monthly categories into presentation columns.

00:00:31.762 --> 00:00:37.332
The technical feature matters because it changes what questions we can answer reliably and how easily another

00:00:37.332 --> 00:00:40.997
analyst can understand our work.

00:00:40.997 --> 00:00:45.827
As you listen, try to connect each SQL or data concept to a decision you might need to

00:00:45.827 --> 00:00:52.157
defend later: what the data means, what one row represents, what can be missing,

00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:56.320
and what assumptions the transformation introduces.
